// ============================================================================
// deepspatch.dl -- deep dispatch through registries that the runtime populates
// reflectively.
//
// A registry names implementation classes that the program instantiates
// reflectively and then uses through a service type: java.util.ServiceLoader
// (classes named in META-INF/services/I), or a name->class factory
// (`(Action) actions.getObjectOfClass(name)`). A static call graph loses every
// product, and with it everything downstream of it.
//
// deepspatch binds the registered products into the analysis so that calling
// product methods dispatches to the real product bodies. It is organised as one
// back-end fed by front-ends:
//
//   deepspatch/dispatch-backend.dl          uniform back-end: product mocks, the
//                                           COARSE tier (products stand in for the
//                                           service type wherever it is mocked) and
//                                           the PRECISE tier (bind the result of each
//                                           reached registry call, in the caller's
//                                           context: Iterable, Iterator or instance)
//   deepspatch/frontend-service-loader.dl   ServiceLoader and reimplementations;
//                                           fully automatic, from the ServiceProvider
//                                           facts fact generation emits
//   deepspatch/frontend-reflective-factory.dl
//                                           name->class factories, from optional
//                                           ReflectiveFactory* input facts
//
// Front-ends only state WHAT a registry can produce (DispatchProduct) and WHERE a
// reached call asks for it (DispatchCall); see dispatch-backend.dl for the
// contract. To support another kind of registry, add a front-end that derives
// those two relations and include it below.
//
// Included at top level after the mocking layer (like spring-data-repo), so it
// uses the mainAnalysis.* component-qualified relations. It is preprocessed
// standalone (CPreprocessor.includeAtEnd), so it #includes the macro header it
// needs; the parts below are #included into this one unit. Guarded to analyses
// that instantiate mainAnalysis (SouffleAnalysis).
// ============================================================================
#include "../commonMacros.dl"

#include "deepspatch/dispatch-backend.dl"
#include "deepspatch/frontend-service-loader.dl"
#include "deepspatch/frontend-reflective-factory.dl"
